// A gate that can NEVER be active gates dead code, so it is a mistake rather than a declaration nobody
// compiles. `DEBUG` and `RELEASE` are two values of BUILD_TYPE, and a single-select group has exactly one
// value per build — so no configuration in any product of flags reaches this body.
//
// Refused in `pruneInactiveDecls`, where every gate passes, so `kama build`, `kama check` and the language
// server all say it. That is the difference between this and a gate merely out of reach of every declared
// target (`@compileFor(ARCH_RISCV64)` with no riscv target): that one is stub code for a platform this
// project does not support yet, is checked the day the target is declared, and is NOT an error.
@compileFor(DEBUG, RELEASE)
fn int32 unreachableEverywhere() { return 251; }

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
